foundation.question_text:
$\triangle PQR$ has been translated to give the second triangle.
Write a congruence statement for the two triangles.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.3,0.3);
\coordinate (R) at (0.8,1.6);
\coordinate (T) at (3.3,0.5);
\coordinate (U) at (5.6,0.8);
\coordinate (V) at (4.1,2.1);
\draw (P) -- (Q) -- (R) -- cycle;
\draw (T) -- (U) -- (V) -- cycle;
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above] at (R) {$R$};
\node[below left] at (T) {$T$};
\node[below right] at (U) {$U$};
\node[above] at (V) {$V$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

